    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> was crowned Emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a> on 16 April 1346, a title that claimed the succession of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dusans-code">Dušan's Code</a>, enacted in 1349 and 1354, had 201 articles based on Roman-Byzantine law and is considered a medieval constitution.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-uros-v">Stefan Uroš V</a> the empire fragmented into principalities, and it effectively ended with his death in 1371, the year of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maritsa">Battle of Maritsa</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> did not fight a single field battle to win his empire: he took it by besieging cities.</p></aside>
    </section>

